This useEffect responds to screen focus changes by executing navigation logic. The navigation should be triggered directly when the condition is met, not deferred through state updates and focus tracking.

**Suggested fix:**

Remove the `shouldNavigateOnFocus` state and the second useEffect. Instead, add `isFocused` to the dependency array of this effect. The effect will naturally re-run when `isFocused` changes, and you can check both conditions inline:

```tsx
const prevValidatedDate = usePrevious(loginData?.validatedDate);
const isFocused = useIsFocused();

useEffect(() => {
    // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/prefer-nullish-coalescing
    if (prevValidatedDate || \!loginData?.validatedDate) {
        return;
    }

    if (\!isFocused) {
        return;
    }

    // Navigate to methods page on successful magic code verification.
    // The validatedDate property indicates successful magic code verification.
    Navigation.goBack(ROUTES.SETTINGS_CONTACT_METHODS.getRoute(backTo));
}, [prevValidatedDate, loginData?.validatedDate, isDefaultContactMethod, backTo, isFocused]);
```

This eliminates the unnecessary state management and makes the logic clearer.

